                        2890 --1069:  *  - #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0OMR must have been configured beforehand.
                        2891 --1070:  * \par Detailed description
                        2892 --1071:  *      - Calculates the remainder with an even modulus.
                        2893 --1072:  * \par Remarks
                        2894 --1073:  *  - None
                        2895 --1074:  *
                        2896 --1075:  * Pseudo-code for the function can be found below.
                        2897 --1076:  *  -# Set ret to #PKCD_RET_OK.
                        2898 --1077:  *  -# Set omr to #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0OMR.
                        2899 --1078:  *  -# Set p_wk_a to p_wk1.
                        2900 --1079:  *  -# Set p_wk_mod to p_wk2.
                        2901 --1080:  *  -# Set p_wk_temp to p_wk3.
                        2902 --1081:  *  -# Get the bit length of a with #r_pkcd_cmn_find_msb.
                        2903 --1082:  *  -# Get the bit length of mod with #r_pkcd_cmn_find_msb.
                        2904 --1083:  *  -# Clear p_wk1 with #r_pkcd_cmn_ram_clr.
                        2905 --1084:  *  -# Clear p_wk2 with #r_pkcd_cmn_ram_clr.
                        2906 --1085:  *  -# Clear p_wk3 with #r_pkcd_cmn_ram_clr.
                        2907 --1086:  *  -# Clear p_wk_out with #r_pkcd_cmn_ram_clr.
                        2908 --1087:  *  -# Copy the data at p_a to p_wk_a with #r_pkcd_cmn_cpy_by_64bounds.
                        2909 --1088:  *  -# Copy the modulus at p_mod to p_wk_mod with #r_pkcd_cmn_cpy_by_64bounds.
                        2910 --1089:  *  -# If a_msb >= mod_msb, then
                        2911 --1090:  *    -# Set msb_diff to (a_msb - mod_msb).
                        2912 --1091:  *    -# Set the PKCC DL with #r_pkcd_cmn_set_dl.
